The '''2015–16 network television schedule''' for the five major English-language commercial [[List of United States over-the-air television networks|broadcast networks in the United States]] covers [[prime time]] hours from September 2015 to August 2016. The schedule is followed by a [[#By network|list per network]] of returning series, new series, and series canceled after the [[2014–15 United States network television schedule|2014–15 season]].

[[NBC]] was the first to announce its fall schedule on May 10, 2015,<ref name="NBC Fall 2015">{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/10/nbc-2015-2016-schedule-blindspot-moves-to-post-voice-spot-live-undateable-goes-to-friday-heroes-reborn-gets-pre-blacklist-thursday-spot/401619/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150512030539/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/10/nbc-2015-2016-schedule-blindspot-moves-to-post-voice-spot-live-undateable-goes-to-friday-heroes-reborn-gets-pre-blacklist-thursday-spot/401619/|url-status=dead|archive-date=May 12, 2015|title=NBC 2015–2016 Schedule: 'Blindspot' Gets Post-'Voice' Spot, Live 'Undateable' Goes to Friday, + 'Heroes Reborn' Gets Pre 'Blacklist' Thursday Spot|last=Kondolojy|first=Amanda|work=TV by the Numbers|date=May 10, 2015|access-date=May 10, 2015}}</ref> followed by [[Fox Broadcasting Company|Fox]] on May 11,<ref name="Fox Fall 2015">{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/11/fox-2015-16-schedule-announced-american-idol-to-end-after-15th-season-rosewood-gets-pre-empire-slot-wednesdays/401954/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150513205735/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/11/fox-2015-16-schedule-announced-american-idol-to-end-after-15th-season-rosewood-gets-pre-empire-slot-wednesdays/401954/|url-status=dead|archive-date=May 13, 2015|title=Fox 2015–16 Schedule Announced: 'American Idol' to End After 15th Season, 'Rosewood' Gets Pre 'Empire' Slot Wednesday, 'The X Files' to Premiere in January|last=Bibel|first=Sara|work=TV by the Numbers|date=May 11, 2015|access-date=May 11, 2015}}</ref> [[American Broadcasting Company|ABC]] on May 12,<ref>{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/12/abc-2015-16-primetime-schedule-the-muppets-on-tuesday-dr-ken-friday-of-kings-prophets-oil-on-sunday/402964/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150514164017/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/12/abc-2015-16-primetime-schedule-the-muppets-on-tuesday-dr-ken-friday-of-kings-prophets-oil-on-sunday/402964/|url-status=dead|archive-date=May 14, 2015|title=ABC 2015–16 Primetime Schedule: 'The Muppets' & 'Quantico' on Tuesday, 'Of Kings & Prophets' & 'Oil' on Sunday, 'Wicked City'|last=Bibel|first=Sara|work=TV by the Numbers|date=May 12, 2015|access-date=May 12, 2015}}</ref> [[CBS]] on May 13,<ref name="CBS Fall 2015">{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/13/cbs-2015-16-primetime-schedule-supergirl-to-monday-in-november/403498/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150516000405/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/13/cbs-2015-16-primetime-schedule-supergirl-to-monday-in-november/403498/|url-status=dead|archive-date=May 16, 2015|title=CBS 2015–16 Primetime Schedule: 'Supergirl' to Monday in November, 'Limitless' on Tuesday, 'Code Black' Wednesday, 'CSI' Finale on September 27 'Rush Hour' & 'Criminal Minds: Beyond Borders' Held for Midseason|last=Bibel|first=Sara|work=TV by the Numbers|date=May 13, 2015|access-date=May 13, 2015}}</ref> and [[The CW]] on May 14.<ref name="CW Fall 2015">{{cite web|url=http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/14/cw-2015-16-primetime-schedule-the-flash-arrow-retain-timeslots-crazy-ex-girlfriend-opens-monday-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-to-midseason-reign-on-fridays/404066/|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150516123047/http://tvbythenumbers.zap2it.com/2015/05/14/cw-2015-16-primetime-schedule-the-flash-arrow-retain-timeslots-crazy-ex-girlfriend-opens-monday-dcs-legends-of-tomorrow-to-midseason-reign-on-fridays/404066/|url-status=dead|archive-date=May 16, 2015|title=CW 2015–16 Primetime Schedule: 'The Flash' & 'Arrow' Retain Timeslots, 'Crazy Ex-Girlfriend' Opens Monday, 'DC's Legends of Tomorrow' to Midseason, 'The Originals' Moves to Thursday, 'Reign' on Friday|last=Kondolojy|first=Amanda|work=TV by the Numbers|date=May 14, 2015|access-date=May 14, 2015}}</ref>

[[PBS]] is not included; member stations have local flexibility over most of their schedules and broadcast times for network shows may vary. [[Ion Television]], [[The CW Plus]], and [[MyNetworkTV]] are also not included since the majority of the networks' schedules comprise syndicated reruns (with limited original programming on the latter two). [[The CW]] is not included on weekends, since it does not offer network programming.

New series are highlighted in '''bold'''.

All times are [[Eastern Time Zone|U.S. Eastern]] and [[Pacific Time Zone|Pacific time]] (except for some live sports or events). Subtract one hour for [[Central Time Zone|Central]] and [[Mountain Time Zone|Mountain]] times.

'''Note''': From August 5 to August 21, 2016, all NBC primetime programming was pre-empted for coverage of the [[2016 Summer Olympics]] in [[Rio de Janeiro]], [[Brazil]].

Each of the 30 highest-rated shows is listed with its rank and rating as determined by [[Nielsen Media Research]].<ref name="BM2">Highest-rated series is based on the annual top-rated programs list compiled by [[Nielsen Media Research]] and reported on [http://www.timbrooks.net/ratings/ TimBrooks.net/Ratings]</ref>

